Fundamentals
  LLM          : large language model (next-token predictor)
  Prompt       : input text that steers generation
  Context      : tokens the model can attend to in one pass
  Token        : discrete text unit the model actually sees

Core types / variables you keep running into
  model        : the weights + architecture
  context_window : max tokens in one request
  temperature  : randomness of sampling
  system_prompt : persistent instructions
  tools        : functions the model is allowed to call
  tool_schema  : JSON / typed description of those functions
  messages     : conversation history (role + content)
  embedding    : dense vector of a chunk of text
  vector_db    : store + search those embeddings
  rag          : retrieve relevant chunks, then generate
  agent        : loop of think → act (tool) → observe
  memory       : short-term (context) + long-term (store)
  guardrail    : filter / policy that constrains output
  eval         : tests that measure quality / safety / cost
